AWS Tip of the Day – ELB Types

Amazon Web Services provides 4 types of Load Balancers:

* ALB (Application Load Balancer) – Layer 7, for HTTP/HTTPS web apps
* NLB (Network Load Balancer) – Layer 4, for high-speed TCP/UDP traffic
* GWLB (Gateway Load Balancer) – Used for firewalls and security appliances
* CLB (Classic Load Balancer) – Older generation, mainly for legacy apps

Quick Tip

ALB = Web Apps | NLB = Performance | GWLB = Security | CLB = Legacy
